      "issues": [
        "Fetch official supporting evidence for: The Indian Constitution works the same way. Parliament can amend (change) almost anything—like adding new rules or fixing small mistakes. But the Supreme Court said in the famous Kesavananda Bharati case (1973) that Parliament cannot destroy the \"basic structure\" of the Constitution. The basic structure is like the soul of the club—without it, the Constitution would become something completely different."
      ],
